cat <<'EOF'
Installing Bingux OS
====================

1. Connect to the network. Ethernet and known Wi-Fi networks connect on their
   own; for Wi-Fi run nmtui.
2. Find the disk to install onto:
       lsblk
3. Install. This ERASES the disk, so check the name twice:
       bingux-os-install --disk /dev/DISK --user NAME
   The installer asks for a password and then for the disk name to confirm.
   Use --help for the hostname, timezone, locale and keyboard options.
4. Reboot, remove the USB stick, and sign in at the Bingux login screen.

Anything the installer does not cover (encryption, other layouts, extra
packages) can be done with archinstall; add the bingux-os package to its
additional packages.

Project and documentation: https://github.com/kierandrewett/bingux
EOF
